Identity Operations will validate the session-cache failover procedure on
Monday, 20 Jul, from 09:00 to 09:25 UTC. This is a controlled maintenance
exercise following the cache-recovery action noted during the 2026-07-13
operations review.

The team will move one cache shard through the documented standby path while
watching sign-in success, token-refresh latency, and cache eviction rate. The
exercise does not change account data, customer profiles, or authentication
policy. Northstar Transit Cloud support staff should expect a brief increase in
background session refreshes but no planned interactive sign-in interruption.

SRE On-Call will have the rollback procedure and the identity on-call runbook
open before the window begins. If sign-in success drops below the maintenance
guardrail for three minutes, Identity Operations will stop the exercise and
restore the original shard placement.

A concise result note, including observed timings and any follow-up action,
will be sent to this list by 12:00 UTC on 20 Jul.
